From 3896cddc2524b6a381d24f2d3ef289030a5fa1fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: genspark_dev <genspark_dev@genspark.ai>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 01:55:18 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Make the seal cover the letter itself, and make amending it
 attributable

The snapshot omitted the body, its due date and the concerned person, so the
text of a sealed letter could be rewritten with no trace. Include them, and
read the record's own seal state when verification finds no snapshot.

Give the seal a documented exit: reopening now requires a reason, records the
previous snapshot in the activity trail, and lifts the seal, so a corrected
record is amended in the open rather than silently.

Freeze the approval decision on the server. read_only is not enforced there,
which left the recorded approver forgeable and the timestamp backdatable.
